{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473398-hecata-homebrew-lore-sheet","id":1473398,"title":"Hecata Homebrew Lore Sheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-27T05:50:51-08:00","id":1473398,"title":"Hecata Homebrew Lore Sheet","content":"I got a homebrew lore sheet I want to share with the community.<br /> <br /> <b>Binder of Ghosts</b><br /> (Hecata Characters Only)<br /> <br /> Morgues. Graveyards. Catacombs. Battlefields. Anywhere death left its mark ghosts congregate, and you know exactly how to leverage this phenomena for your benefit. You have ghostly servants whom you've bargained with, bound, or bullied into service. They perform favors that living servants cannot. You must be careful, however, as many do not look kindly on those who abuse the dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Grave Secrets:</b> Even secrets taken to the grave can still be unearthed. Once per story, you can ask the Storyteller about a secret regarding a deceased character and they must answer truthfully.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ghostly Servants:</b> You have a network of ghostly servants and spies who either willingly trade information and favors with you or you make them do so through force. Whichever way, you can distribute 3 dots between Retainer and Contacts, but you also gain one Mythic Flaw, as surrounding yourself with death has unnatural consequences.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghostly Watchman:</b> You have bound a ghost to protect your Haven. This unseen servitor is a terrifying guardian for all who dare to step into your resting place. This counts as a Spectre (see p. 377 of the Core book) but the concentration of deathly energy also gives your Haven the Creepy Flaw.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lady in Black:</b> Almost everywhere in the world a shade called the Lady in Black appears to necromancers. She is always a woman veiled in a dark robe whose ethnicity matches the locale. She is often found in graveyards and crossroads, and can teach you one Oblivion Ritual of your choosing, once per story. This isn't without cost, as the Lady always demands some sort of task performed in exchange for her tutelage.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pyriphlegethon:</b> You've come upon one of the most complex and loathed rituals of Oblivion. This vile ceremony allows you to completely obliterate a character's soul and replace it with a slave-spirit bound to your will, ultimately creating a puppet servant. This is a Level 5 ritual, work with your Storyteller to figure out the details of the Ingredients and Process, but they must be highly challenging. Furthermore, each casting of this ritual inflicts 5 Stains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}